From: bloqaudio <qoshea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: NAK OUT endpoints until a request is
 queued

dwc2_hsotg_ep_enable() sets SNAK only for isochronous OUT endpoints. A
bulk or interrupt OUT endpoint comes up active with NAK clear, so until
the function driver queues its first request the core ACKs OUT data and
writes it into the RX FIFO. That FIFO is shared by every OUT endpoint;
in DMA mode nothing drains an entry for an endpoint with no descriptor
armed, and every later OUT packet, EP0 SETUPs included, queues behind it.

u_serial queues ACM OUT requests only when the tty is opened. A host
that writes to the ACM port first, as ModemManager's probe does, wedges
the whole gadget: on an SG2002 (DWC_otg 4.20a, descriptor DMA), three
bytes of "AT\r" left GRXSTSR pointing at a 3-byte packet on the idle
ACM endpoint, the next CDC-ECM SET_ETHERNET_PACKET_FILTER never
completed, and ECM bulk OUT stopped for good.

Set SNAK on every non-EP0 OUT endpoint when it is enabled.
dwc2_hsotg_start_req() already clears the NAK when it arms a request,
and dwc2_hsotg_ep_disable() sets it again.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -4156,6 +4156,15 @@ static int dwc2_hsotg_ep_enable(struct usb_ep *ep,
 	}
 
 	/*
+	 * NAK OUT tokens until a request is queued; dwc2_hsotg_start_req()
+	 * clears the NAK. Otherwise the core accepts a packet into the RX
+	 * FIFO, which all OUT endpoints share, and in DMA mode nothing drains
+	 * it: every OUT endpoint, EP0 SETUPs included, stalls behind it.
+	 */
+	if (!dir_in && index)
+		epctrl |= DXEPCTL_SNAK;
+
+	/*
 	 * if the hardware has dedicated fifos, we must give each IN EP
 	 * a unique tx-fifo even if it is non-periodic.
 	 */
-- 
2.53.0
